PROJECT_STEPS=[
 [r'Write A = (x² + 4)¹⁰, B = sin⁵√x and C = (1 + cos x)⁻¹/², so the function is ABC.',r'The real source domain is x ≥ 0 and 1 + cos x > 0. For ordinary chain differentiation take x > 0; sin√x = 0 is allowed.',r'Differentiate A: A′ = 20x(x² + 4)⁹. Differentiate B: B′ = 5sin⁴√x cos√x/(2√x).',r'Differentiate C: C′ = sin x/[2(1 + cos x)³/²].',r'Product rule gives A′BC + AB′C + ABC′. This direct sum remains valid at positive zeros of sin√x, unlike a logarithmic-derivative form that divides by sin√x.',r'The three terms are 20x(x² + 4)⁹sin⁵√x/√(1 + cos x), plus 5(x² + 4)¹⁰sin⁴√x cos√x/[2√x√(1 + cos x)], plus (x² + 4)¹⁰sin⁵√x sin x/[2(1 + cos x)³/²].',r'At x = 0, use the right derivative separately: sin⁵√x behaves as x⁵/², so the function’s right derivative is zero. This limit is not a two-sided derivative on the real source domain.',r'A software request is diff((x^2+4)^10*sin(sqrt(x))^5/sqrt(1+cos(x)),x); the expression above is its independently derived expected derivative.'],
 [r'Write U = √(1 + csc x), A = (x² + 4)⁻¹⁰ and B = sin⁻⁵√x, so the function is UAB.',r'The real source domain requires x > 0, sin x ≠ 0, sin√x ≠ 0 and 1 + csc x ≥ 0. For a smooth interval assume the last expression is strictly positive.',r'U′ = −csc x cot x/[2√(1 + csc x)]; A′ = −20x(x² + 4)⁻¹¹.',r'B′ = −5cos√x/[2√x sin⁶√x].',r'The derivative is U′AB + UA′B + UAB′: −csc x cot x/[2√(1 + csc x)(x² + 4)¹⁰sin⁵√x], minus 20x√(1 + csc x)/[(x² + 4)¹¹sin⁵√x], minus 5√(1 + csc x)cos√x/[2√x(x² + 4)¹⁰sin⁶√x].',r'At a source-domain point where sin x = −1, the numerator U is zero. Locally 1 + csc x is negative on either side, so there is no real open interval on which the source function is defined; the displayed smooth derivative does not apply there.',r'A software request is diff(sqrt(1+csc(x))/((x^2+4)^10*sin(sqrt(x))^5),x); keep the original domain exclusions when simplifying its expected output.']
]
